<li about="#cite_note-70" id="cite_note-70" data-mw-footnote-number="70"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBiA"><a href="#cite_ref-70" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBiE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBiI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-70" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt236" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBiM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"http://torrentfreak.com/microsoft-censors-pirate-bay-links-in-windows-live-messenger-120324/"},"title":{"wt":"Microsoft Censors Pirate Bay Links in Windows Live Messenger"},"first":{"wt":"Ernesto"},"last":{"wt":"Van Der Sar"},"work":{"wt":"[[TorrentFreak]]"},"date":{"wt":"March 24, 2012"},"access-date":{"wt":"April 1, 2012"},"quote":{"wt":"Whatever Microsoft&apos;s reason for monitoring private conversations and then swallowing Pirate Bay links, the Redmond-based company&apos;s censorship policies are not very consistent. All of the other large BitTorrent sites remain unaffected, even though they offer content that&apos;s identical to The Pirate Bay."},"archive-date":{"wt":"March 29, 2012"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20120329095617/http://torrentfreak.com/microsoft-censors-pirate-bay-links-in-windows-live-messenger-120324/"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFVan_Der_Sar2012" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt236">Van Der Sar, Ernesto (March 24, 2012). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://torrentfreak.com/microsoft-censors-pirate-bay-links-in-windows-live-messenger-120324/" class="external text" id="mwBiQ">"Microsoft Censors Pirate Bay Links in Windows Live Messenger"</a>. <i id="mwBiU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TorrentFreak" title="TorrentFreak" id="mwBiY">TorrentFreak</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120329095617/http://torrentfreak.com/microsoft-censors-pirate-bay-links-in-windows-live-messenger-120324/" class="external text" id="mwBic">Archived</a> from the original on March 29, 2012<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwBig">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwBik">April 1,</span> 2012</span>. <q id="mwBio">Whatever Microsoft's reason for monitoring private conversations and then swallowing Pirate Bay links, the Redmond-based company's censorship policies are not very consistent. All of the other large BitTorrent sites remain unaffected, even though they offer content that's identical to The Pirate Bay.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=TorrentFreak&amp;rft.atitle=Microsoft+Censors+Pirate+Bay+Links+in+Windows+Live+Messenger&amp;rft.date=2012-03-24&amp;rft.aulast=Van+Der+Sar&amp;rft.aufirst=Ernesto&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Ftorrentfreak.com%2Fmicrosoft-censors-pirate-bay-links-in-windows-live-messenger-120324%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AMSN+Messenger" class="Z3988" about="#mwt236" id="mwBis"></span></span></li>
